.policy "python-security-orm-lookup-injection" revision 1
.description "Let the client choose Django ORM lookup values only, never lookup keys or field names: keep request-chosen names to an allow-list."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. It reports a Django ORM call where the client picks the lookup or field names, not
// just the values, in the same function or through the project's helpers in other files:
//   - a mapping whose keys come from the request expanded with `**` into `filter`, `exclude`, `get`,
//     `get_or_create`, `update_or_create`, `annotate`, `alias`, `aggregate`, `values`, `order_by` (any receiver:
//     the method name and the request-keyed splat are enough), into `update` on a queryset receiver (a plain
//     dict's `update(**…)` is common), or into `django.db.models.Q(**…)`. Request-keyed: the request mapping itself
//     (`request.GET`, `.dict()`, `.copy()`, `request.data`, `request.data["filters"]`), a dict literal or
//     comprehension with a request-derived key (`{f"{field}__icontains": v}`, `{k: v for k, v in
//     request.GET.items()}`), a name filled by `d[key] = …` with such a key or by `d.update(<request mapping>)`;
//   - a request string passed as a field name to `order_by`, `values`, `values_list`, `only`, `defer` (positional or
//     `*`-splatted) on a queryset receiver, or to `F(name)`, `Trunc(…, kind)`, `Extract(…, lookup_name)` (Django
//     CVE-2021-35042, CVE-2022-34265, CVE-2024-42005). A free-text value of a form's `cleaned_data` or a
//     serializer's `validated_data` (`CharField`, `ListField(child=CharField())`) counts as request text.
// Queryset receivers are resolved, not guessed from names: a chain from `.objects`/`_default_manager`,
// `get_queryset()`, `filter_queryset()`, `.queryset`; a related manager of a model of the run (a ForeignKey's or
// ManyToManyField's `related_name`, `<model>_set`, a ManyToManyField's own name); a name bound to one; the return of
// a function of the run that returns one; a parameter that some call of the run passes one to (any name: `items`,
// `objects`, `books`); the queryset parameter of a DRF or django-filter hook (`filter_queryset`,
// `paginate_queryset`) in a subclass of the framework's class.
//   def search(request):
//       Book.objects.filter(**request.GET.dict())                          reported
//       Book.objects.filter(title__icontains=request.GET["q"])            not reported: the value is a parameter
//   (views.py) helpers.apply_sort(Book.objects.all(), request.GET["sort"])
//   (helpers.py) def apply_sort(items, sort): return items.order_by(sort)  reported, naming views.py's line
// Sanitisers it trusts: a name its function tests with `in` / `not in` or passes to a validator-named call
// (lib/security's sec_checked: `if sort not in ALLOWED: …`, `{k: v for k, v in request.GET.items() if k in
// ALLOWED}`, `sort = sanitize_order_by(sort, …)`), the same expression text checked in the function
// (sec_checked_expr), a name passed to `Model._meta.get_field(name)`, a field-name sink inside an `if`/`elif`
// that tests the name, or one derived from it, with `in` or `==` (`order_field = ordering.lstrip("-")`; `elif
// order_field in (…): qs.order_by(ordering)`), a dict lookup (`SORTS[request.GET["sort"]]`, `SORTS.get(…)`), a
// validator-named helper's return, a typed validated value (lib/security's sec_typed: a choice, number, boolean,
// UUID or date field); for a `**` splat, a form's `cleaned_data` or a serializer's `validated_data` (its keys are
// the declared fields), and a check of every key of the same request mapping in the same function (`for k in
// request.GET: if k not in ALLOWED: raise`, also over `.keys()`/`.items()`, `set(request.GET) - ALLOWED`,
// `set(request.GET) <= ALLOWED`, `.issubset(ALLOWED)`).
// Left alone: keyword lookups with request values (`filter(title__icontains=q)`) and dicts with fixed keys and
// request values (`filter(**{"title__icontains": q})`): Django parameterises values; `**kwargs` and the keys of
// `self.kwargs` (the URLconf's capture names); server-built dicts; `create(**request.data)` (mass assignment: the drf
// pack); `order_by(x)` on a receiver not resolved to a queryset (`Table().order_by(x)`, a parameter only ever given
// a table); a field name under `if "<text>" in name:` (only names holding that text pass); test files; staff-only
// code, where the client is staff who already see and sort the admin's data: lib/security's sec_xadmin_fn (a
// function that rejects when `not request.user.is_staff`/`is_superuser`, `@staff_member_required`,
// `@user_passes_test(lambda u: u.is_staff)`, `@permission_required(…)`, DRF `@permission_classes([IsAdminUser])`,
// `method_decorator` of a staff decorator, ModelAdmin/AdminSite methods, a DRF view with IsAdminUser, methods of a
// class with an admin-only `dispatch`, a staff-only `test_func`, `PermissionRequiredMixin`, an InlineModelAdmin or
// list filter, resolved through bases), a call under `if request.user.is_staff:`, and a helper every call of which
// comes from such a function (two levels deep).
// Overlap: none in Ruff or Bandit; Semgrep's `django/security/injection/mass-assignment` covers only
// `objects.create(**request.X)` and `update(**request.X)` followed by `save()`, not lookups or ordering.
// Gaps: lib/security's (values stored on objects or read back from the database, such as a saved view's filters,
// are not followed; calls the call graph cannot resolve); a check in a caller clears a helper's parameter only when
// it checks the argument it passes; the `in` / validator / key-loop checks are flow-insensitive (a test anywhere in
// the function counts); a queryset reached only through an unresolved call or an attribute of an object that is not
// a related manager's name (`self.items`) is not a receiver; the library admin and staff bases outside the run are a
// name list (Django's own, `braces`' `StaffuserRequiredMixin`/`SuperuserRequiredMixin`, and any base from an `admin`
// module named `…Admin`/`…Inline`/`…ListFilter`); a helper is staff-only only when the call graph sees every call
// of it; `QuerySet.extra(order_by=…)` is the sql-injection rule's.

#include "lib/security.rerail"

// Per file and across files (lib/security's origins): each file states what its ORM calls take by origin
// (sec_fhit, keyed by the splat or the field-name argument), and a finding reads the cross-file answer by that
// node's term (sec_xfirst): its first source. A queryset receiver a helper of another file returns or is passed, and
// a related manager another file's model declares, are yes/no origins (sec_bres); staff-only functions are decided
// over the call graph by symbol (olk_xstaff).
.violation LookupKeys(at: node, what: symbol, p: symbol, l: number) "ORM lookup names chosen by {what} ({p}:{l}): keep only allow-listed keys, or pass request values to fixed lookups. Leave it if the keys were checked against an allow-list in another function."
LookupKeys(c, what, p, l) :- olk_splat(c, a, q), sec_bres(q), pt_tm(a, at), !olk_xcleared(at), pt_tm(c, ct),
    !olk_xstaff_at(ct), sec_xfirst("olkL", at, k), sec_src_info(k, what, p, l).
sec_fhit("olkL", a, o) :- olk_splat(c, a, _), olk_keys(a, o), olk_live(c).
.violation FieldName(at: node, what: symbol, p: symbol, l: number) "Field name from {what} ({p}:{l}) reaches the ORM: map it through a dict of fixed names or an allow-list (DRF: OrderingFilter with ordering_fields). Leave it if the name was already checked."
FieldName(c, what, p, l) :- olk_name_arg(c, v, q), sec_bres(q), pt_tm(c, ct), !olk_xstaff_at(ct), pt_tm(v, vt),
    sec_xfirst("olkF", vt, k), sec_src_info(k, what, p, l).
sec_fhit("olkF", v, o) :- olk_name_arg(c, v, _), !sec_checked_expr(v), !olk_guarded(c, v), olk_live(c), olk_str(v, o),
    !sec_echk_any("sec", v).
sec_fhit("olkF", v, g) :- olk_name_arg(c, v, _), !sec_checked_expr(v), !olk_guarded(c, v), olk_live(c), olk_str(v, _),
    sec_egate("sec", "olks", v, g).
sec_gin(g, o) :- olk_name_arg(_, v, _), olk_str(v, o), sec_egate("sec", "olks", v, g).
// olk_live(c): sink call c is outside test code and under no `if <user>.is_staff:`.
.decl olk_live(c: node)
olk_live(c) :- (olk_splat(c, _, _) ; olk_name_arg(c, _, _)), docof(c, d), !sec_test_doc(d), !olk_staff_if(c).
// A source read in staff-only code was sent by staff.
sec_xdrop(r, k) :- (r = "olkL" ; r = "olkF"), olk_xstaff_src(k).
sec_flavor("olks"). sec_flavor("olkk"). sec_flavor("olkq").

// olk_guarded(c, v): call c sits in the body of an `if`/`elif` whose test compares, with `in` or `==`, a name that
// sink value v reads or a name derived from one (`order_field = ordering.lstrip("-")` then `elif order_field in
// ("name", "owner__username"): qs.order_by(ordering)`), or tests that the name contains fixed text (`if
// "date_created" in orderby:`: only names holding that text get through).
.decl olk_guarded(c: node, v: node)
olk_guarded(c, v) :- olk_name_arg(c, v, _), py_if(_, t, b), within(c, b), olk_test_name(t, y),
    nearest(c, h, fscope), olk_derived(h, y, x), olk_val_reads(v, x).
.decl olk_test_name(t: node, y: symbol)
olk_test_name(t, y) :- olk_test_left(t, a), sec_reads(a, y).
olk_test_name(t, y) :- unparen(t, k), olk_has_test(k, y).
olk_test_name(t, y) :- has(t, k, "comparison_operator"), olk_has_test(k, y).
// olk_has_test(k, y): comparison k is `"<text>" in y`.
.decl olk_has_test(k: node, y: symbol)
olk_has_test(k, y) :- kind(k, "comparison_operator"), op(k, "in"), child(k, l, 0), kind(l, "string"), child(k, r0, i),
    i > 0, unparen(r0, r), kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, y).
.decl olk_test_left(t: node, a: node)
olk_test_left(t, a) :- unparen(t, k), olk_eq_test(k, a).
olk_test_left(t, a) :- has(t, k, "comparison_operator"), olk_eq_test(k, a).
.decl olk_eq_test(k: node, a: node)
olk_eq_test(k, a) :- kind(k, "comparison_operator"), op(k, o), (o = "in" ; o = "=="), child(k, a, 0).
// olk_derived(h, y, x): in scope h, name y is x, or is bound to an expression that reads x.
.decl olk_derived(h: node, y: symbol, x: symbol)
olk_derived(h, y, y) :- olk_guard_name(h, y).
olk_derived(h, y, x) :- olk_guard_name(h, y), sec_bind(h, y, e), has(e, i, "identifier"), text(i, x),
    !field(_, "attribute", i).
olk_derived(h, y, x) :- olk_guard_name(h, y), sec_bind(h, y, e), kind(e, "identifier"), text(e, x).
.decl olk_guard_name(h: node, y: symbol)
olk_guard_name(h, y) :- olk_name_arg(c, _, _), py_if(_, t, b), within(c, b), olk_test_name(t, y),
    nearest(c, h, fscope).
.decl olk_val_reads(v: node, x: symbol)
olk_val_reads(v, x) :- olk_name_arg(_, v, _), kind(v, "identifier"), text(v, x).
olk_val_reads(v, x) :- olk_name_arg(_, v, _), has(v, i, "identifier"), text(i, x), !field(_, "attribute", i).

// ---- sinks ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// olk_splat(c, a, q): call c expands mapping a with `**` into lookup or field names; on a queryset receiver for
// `update` (q its yes/no origin, olk_qs), else q "T".
.decl olk_splat(c: node, a: node, q: symbol)
olk_splat(c, a, "T") :- olk_kwsplat(c, a), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, m), olk_splat_method(m).
olk_splat(c, a, q) :- olk_kwsplat(c, a), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, r0, "update"), unparen(r0, r), olk_qs(r, q).
olk_splat(c, a, "T") :- olk_kwsplat(c, a), sec_call_q(c, q), (q = "django.db.models.Q" ;
    q = "django.db.models.query_utils.Q").
.decl olk_splat_method(m: symbol)
olk_splat_method("filter"). olk_splat_method("exclude"). olk_splat_method("get"). olk_splat_method("get_or_create").
olk_splat_method("update_or_create"). olk_splat_method("annotate"). olk_splat_method("alias").
olk_splat_method("aggregate"). olk_splat_method("values"). olk_splat_method("order_by").
.decl olk_kwsplat(c: node, a: node)
olk_kwsplat(c, a) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "arguments", al), child(al, sp, _), kind(sp, "dictionary_splat"),
    child(sp, a0, 0), unparen(a0, a).

// olk_name_arg(c, v, q): v is a field name, lookup or kind that call c hands to the ORM: a queryset method's (q the
// receiver's yes/no origin, olk_qs), or `F`, `Trunc`, `Extract`'s (q "T").
.decl olk_name_arg(c: node, v: node, q: symbol)
olk_name_arg(c, v, q) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, r0, m), olk_name_method(m), unparen(r0, r),
    olk_qs(r, q), olk_pos_item(c, v).
olk_name_arg(c, v, "T") :- sec_call_q(c, q), (q = "django.db.models.F" ; q = "django.db.models.expressions.F"),
    (sec_arg(c, 0, "", v) ; sec_arg(c, -1, "name", v)).
olk_name_arg(c, v, "T") :- sec_call_q(c, q), (q = "django.db.models.functions.Trunc" ;
    q = "django.db.models.functions.datetime.Trunc"), (sec_arg(c, 1, "", v) ; sec_arg(c, -1, "kind", v)).
olk_name_arg(c, v, "T") :- sec_call_q(c, q), (q = "django.db.models.functions.Extract" ;
    q = "django.db.models.functions.datetime.Extract"), (sec_arg(c, 1, "", v) ; sec_arg(c, -1, "lookup_name", v)).
.decl olk_name_method(m: symbol)
olk_name_method("order_by"). olk_name_method("values"). olk_name_method("values_list"). olk_name_method("only").
olk_name_method("defer").
// olk_pos_item(c, v): v is a positional argument of call c, or what a `*` splat in its arguments expands.
.decl olk_pos_item(c: node, v: node)
olk_pos_item(c, v) :- sec_arg(c, i, "", v), i >= 0.
olk_pos_item(c, v) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "arguments", al), child(al, sp, _), kind(sp, "list_splat"),
    child(sp, v0, 0), unparen(v0, v).

// olk_qs(r, q): receiver r is a Django queryset or manager, or a chain from one, by yes/no origin q: `.objects` and
// the like, `get_queryset()`, a framework hook's queryset parameter (q "T"); a related manager of a model of the run
// (`RN|<name>`, olk_rel_name in the model's file); a name bound to one; a parameter some call of the run passes one
// (`P|olkq|…`); a call of a function of the run that returns one (`R|olkq|…`).
.decl olk_qs(r: node, q: symbol)
olk_qs(r, q) :- olk_qs_head(r, q).
olk_qs(r, q) :- chain_below(r, p), olk_qs_head(p, q).
.decl olk_qs_head(p: node, q: symbol)
olk_qs_head(p, "T") :- attr_of(p, _, a), (a = "objects" ; a = "all_objects" ; a = "_default_manager" ;
    a = "_base_manager" ; a = "queryset").
olk_qs_head(p, cat("RN|", a)) :- attr_of(p, _, a).
olk_qs_head(p, "T") :- kind(p, "call"), call_name(p, m), (m = "get_queryset" ; m = "filter_queryset").
olk_qs_head(p, q) :- kind(p, "identifier"), text(p, x), look(p, x, h), sec_bind(h, x, v), unparen(v, w), w != p,
    olk_qs(w, q).
olk_qs_head(p, q) :- sec_porig(p, "olkq", _, _, q).
olk_qs_head(p, "T") :- kind(p, "identifier"), text(p, x), look(p, x, g), olk_qs_hook_param(g, x).
olk_qs_head(p, q) :- kind(p, "call"), sec_rorig(p, "olkq", q).
sec_bpass("olkq", c, a, q) :- call_arg(c, _, _, a), unparen(a, w), olk_qs(w, q).
sec_bret("olkq", g, q) :- kind(r, "return_statement"), child(r, v, 0), nearest(r, g, fdef), unparen(v, w), olk_qs(w, q).
sec_bres(cat("RN|", a)) :- olk_rel_name(a).
// olk_qs_hook_param(g, x): g is a DRF or django-filter hook the framework calls with a queryset as parameter x: a
// method of a subclass (python/names' class_anc) of a filter backend overriding `filter_queryset(self, request,
// queryset, view)`, or of another framework class (a generic view, a pagination class, a FilterSet) overriding
// `filter_queryset(self, queryset)` / `paginate_queryset(self, queryset, …)`.
.decl olk_qs_hook_param(g: node, x: symbol)
olk_qs_hook_param(g, x) :- def_name(g, "filter_queryset"), nearest(g, k, scope), class_anc(k, b), olk_filter_backend(b),
    param(g, x, 2).
olk_qs_hook_param(g, x) :- def_name(g, m), (m = "filter_queryset" ; m = "paginate_queryset"), nearest(g, k, scope),
    class_anc(k, b), (prefix("rest_framework.", b) ; prefix("django_filters.", b) ; prefix("django.views.", b)),
    !olk_filter_backend(b), param(g, x, 1).
.decl olk_filter_backend(b: symbol)
olk_filter_backend("rest_framework.filters.BaseFilterBackend"). olk_filter_backend("rest_framework.filters.OrderingFilter").
olk_filter_backend("rest_framework.filters.SearchFilter").
olk_filter_backend("django_filters.rest_framework.DjangoFilterBackend").
olk_filter_backend("django_filters.rest_framework.backends.DjangoFilterBackend").
// olk_rel_name(a): attribute a is a related manager of a model of this file: the `related_name` of a ForeignKey or
// ManyToManyField, `<model>_set` for a model with one and no related_name, or a ManyToManyField's own name. By name:
// another file's `obj.<a>` reads it as the origin `RN|<a>`.
.decl olk_rel_name(a: symbol)
olk_rel_name(a) :- olk_rel_field(_, _, v, _), call_arg(v, -1, "related_name", r), str(r, a), a != "+",
    !contains("%(", a).
olk_rel_name(a) :- olk_rel_field(k, _, v, _), !call_arg(v, -1, "related_name", _), field(k, "name", nn), text(nn, n),
    a = cat(@lower(n), "_set").
olk_rel_name(a) :- olk_rel_field(_, a, _, "m2m").
// olk_rel_field(k, x, v, how): model class k of the run declares relation x = v, a ForeignKey ("fk") or a
// ManyToManyField ("m2m").
.decl olk_rel_field(k: node, x: symbol, v: node, how: symbol)
olk_rel_field(k, x, v, how) :- class_anc(k, b), (b = "django.db.models.Model" ; b = "django.db.models.base.Model"),
    asg(k, x, v0, _), unparen(v0, v), kind(v, "call"), field(v, "function", f), sym_of(f, q), olk_rel_q(q, how).
.decl olk_rel_q(q: symbol, how: symbol)
olk_rel_q("django.db.models.ForeignKey", "fk"). olk_rel_q("django.db.models.fields.related.ForeignKey", "fk").
olk_rel_q("django.db.models.ManyToManyField", "m2m").
olk_rel_q("django.db.models.fields.related.ManyToManyField", "m2m").

// ---- staff-only code -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// olk_staff_if(n): n sits under `if <user>.is_staff:`.
.decl olk_staff_if(n: node)
olk_staff_if(n) :- py_if(_, t, b), within(n, b), olk_reads_staff(t), !olk_negated_staff(t).
// olk_xstaff(g): the def whose symbol is g only staff reach: it is admin-only (lib/security's sec_xadmin_fn), or every
// call of it the call graph sees comes from such a function, two levels deep (python/calls' calls, by symbol).
.decl olk_xstaff(g: symbol) cross_file
olk_xstaff(gq) :- olk_xstaff1(gq).
olk_xstaff(gq) :- calls(_, gq), !olk_xopen1(gq).
.decl olk_xopen1(g: symbol) cross_file
olk_xopen1(gq) :- calls(fq, gq), !olk_xstaff1(fq).
.decl olk_xstaff1(g: symbol) cross_file
olk_xstaff1(gq) :- sec_xadmin_fn(gq).
olk_xstaff1(gq) :- calls(_, gq), !olk_xopen0(gq).
.decl olk_xopen0(g: symbol) cross_file
olk_xopen0(gq) :- calls(fq, gq), !sec_xadmin_fn(fq).
// olk_xstaff_at(c): sink call c, by its term, sits in such a function. olk_xstaff_src(k): source k is read in one,
// or under `if <user>.is_staff:` (olk_src_staff_if, in its file).
.decl olk_xstaff_at(c: symbol) cross_file
olk_xstaff_at(ct) :- (olk_splat(c, _, _) ; olk_name_arg(c, _, _)), nearest(c, g, fdef), pt_def(g, gq), olk_xstaff(gq),
    pt_tm(c, ct).
.decl olk_xstaff_src(k: symbol) cross_file
olk_xstaff_src(k) :- sec_src_fn(k, gq), olk_xstaff(gq).
olk_xstaff_src(k) :- olk_src_staff_if(k).
.decl olk_src_staff_if(k: symbol)
olk_src_staff_if(k) :- sec_key(s, k), olk_staff_if(s).
.decl olk_staff_attr(a: symbol)
olk_staff_attr("is_staff"). olk_staff_attr("is_superuser").
// olk_reads_staff(e): e is or contains `<x>.is_staff` / `<x>.is_superuser`.
.decl olk_reads_staff(e: node)
olk_reads_staff(e) :- attr_of(e, _, a), olk_staff_attr(a).
olk_reads_staff(e) :- has(e, x, "attribute"), attr_of(x, _, a), olk_staff_attr(a).
// olk_negated_staff(t): test t negates a staff read (`not request.user.is_staff`, `not (u.is_staff or …)`).
.decl olk_negated_staff(t: node)
olk_negated_staff(t) :- unparen(t, n), kind(n, "not_operator"), olk_reads_staff(n).
olk_negated_staff(t) :- py_if(_, t, _), has(t, n, "not_operator"), olk_reads_staff(n).

// ---- keys checked against an allow-list ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// olk_xcleared(a): splat a, by its term, expands a request mapping whose every key the function reading it checks
// against an allow-list (olk_src_cleared, in the source's file).
.decl olk_xcleared(a: symbol) cross_file
olk_xcleared(at) :- olk_splat(_, a, _), olk_keys(a, o), sec_xres(o, k), olk_src_cleared(k), pt_tm(a, at).
// olk_src_cleared(k): the function that reads source k checks every key of a mapping read off the same request
// mapping, by its text (`request.GET`): olk_keys_checked.
.decl olk_src_cleared(k: symbol)
olk_src_cleared(k) :- sec_key(s2, k), text(s2, t), nearest(s2, h, fscope), olk_keys_checked(h, m), olk_keys(m, k1),
    sec_key(s1, k1), text(s1, t), nearest(s1, h, fscope).
// olk_keys_checked(h, m): scope h checks every key of mapping m: `for k in m: if k not in ALLOWED: raise` (also
// `m.keys()`, `for k, v in m.items()`, a return instead of the raise), `set(m) - ALLOWED`, `set(m) <= ALLOWED`,
// `set(m).issubset(ALLOWED)`, the same on `m.keys()`.
.decl olk_keys_checked(h: node, m: node)
olk_keys_checked(h, m) :- kind(f, "for_statement"), field(f, "left", l), olk_loop_key(l, k), field(f, "right", r0),
    unparen(r0, r), olk_key_iter(r, m), field(f, "body", b), py_if(i, t, ib), within(i, b), unparen(t, ct),
    kind(ct, "comparison_operator"), op(ct, "not in"), child(ct, a, 0), sec_reads(a, k),
    (has(ib, _, "raise_statement") ; has(ib, _, "return_statement")), nearest(f, h, fscope).
olk_keys_checked(h, m) :- olk_key_set(e, m), kind(b, "binary_operator"), op(b, "-"), field(b, "left", e0),
    unparen(e0, e), nearest(b, h, fscope).
olk_keys_checked(h, m) :- olk_key_set(e, m), kind(c, "comparison_operator"), (op(c, "<=") ; op(c, "<")),
    child(c, e0, 0), unparen(e0, e), nearest(c, h, fscope).
olk_keys_checked(h, m) :- olk_key_set(e, m), kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, e0, "issubset"),
    unparen(e0, e), nearest(c, h, fscope).
.decl olk_loop_key(l: node, k: symbol)
olk_loop_key(l, k) :- kind(l, "identifier"), text(l, k).
olk_loop_key(l, k) :- (kind(l, "pattern_list") ; kind(l, "tuple_pattern")), child(l, i, 0), kind(i, "identifier"),
    text(i, k).
// olk_key_iter(r, m): iterating r walks the keys of mapping m: m itself, `m.keys()`, `m.items()`.
.decl olk_key_iter(r: node, m: node)
olk_key_iter(r, m) :- olk_keys(r, _), !kind(r, "call"), m = r.
olk_key_iter(r, m) :- kind(r, "call"), field(r, "function", f), attr_of(f, m0, n), (n = "keys" ; n = "items"),
    unparen(m0, m).
// olk_key_set(e, m): e is the set of mapping m's keys: `set(m)`, `set(m.keys())`, `m.keys()`.
.decl olk_key_set(e: node, m: node)
olk_key_set(e, m) :- kind(e, "call"), sec_call_q(e, "builtins.set"), sec_arg(e, 0, "", a), olk_key_iter(a, m).
olk_key_set(e, m) :- kind(e, "call"), field(e, "function", f), attr_of(f, m0, "keys"), unparen(m0, m).

// ---- names from the request -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// olk_checked_ref(r): name r is read in a function that checks it (sec_checked: an `in` test or a validator-named
// call), or resolves it with `<model>._meta.get_field(name)` (which raises for anything but one of the model's own
// field names, so no `__` path), so its value is taken as one of the allowed names. A check call of the run clears
// it where it reaches no sink of this rule: a name read so passes a gate (sec_ngate "olk", by the name's scope).
.decl olk_checked_ref(r: node)
olk_checked_ref(r) :- kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, x), nearest(r, h, fscope), sec_checked(h, x).
olk_checked_ref(r) :- kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, x), nearest(r, h, fscope), call_name(c, "get_field"),
    sec_arg(c, 0, "", a), unparen(a, i), kind(i, "identifier"), text(i, x), nearest(c, h, fscope).
sec_nchk_c("olk", h, x, t) :- sec_checked_c(h, x, t).
// olk_ref(r, h, x): name r, of x, is read in scope h (nearest), and its function does not surely check it.
.decl olk_ref(r: node, h: node, x: symbol)
olk_ref(r, h, x) :- kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, x), nearest(r, h, fscope), !olk_checked_ref(r).

// olk_str(e, o): e may hold text from origin o that no check stopped: lib/security's taint steps (which stop at a
// typed validated value, sec_typed), a form's `cleaned_data` or a serializer's `validated_data` built from request
// data (a free-text field's value is the client's text), minus the names their function checks, and across calls
// only through arguments the caller did not check (`P|olks|…`, `R|olks|…`).
.decl olk_str(e: node, o: symbol)
olk_str(e, o) :- sec_start(e, o).
olk_str(e, o) :- sec_stepg(e, a), olk_str(a, o).
olk_str(e, g) :- sec_stepq("olks", e, a, g), olk_str(a, _).
sec_gin(g, o) :- sec_stepq("olks", e, a, g), olk_str(a, o).
olk_str(e, o) :- attr_of(e, b, a), sec_validated_attr(a), kind(b, "identifier"), text(b, x), look(b, x, h),
    sec_holder_call(h, x, c), call_arg(c, _, _, v), olk_str(v, o).
olk_str(r, o) :- olk_sin(r, o), olk_ref(r, h, x), !sec_nchk_any("olk", h, x).
olk_str(r, g) :- olk_sin(r, _), olk_ref(r, h, x), sec_ngate("olk", "olks", h, x, g).
sec_gin(g, o) :- olk_sin(r, o), olk_ref(r, h, x), sec_ngate("olk", "olks", h, x, g).
olk_str(c, o) :- sec_rorig(c, "olks", o).
// olk_sin(r, o): name r reads o before its checks: a value bound to it, a parameter's, a route's.
.decl olk_sin(r: node, o: symbol)
olk_sin(r, o) :- kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, x), look(r, x, h), sec_bind(h, x, v), r != v, olk_str(v, o).
olk_sin(r, o) :- sec_porig(r, "olks", _, _, o).
olk_sin(r, k) :- sec_param_ref(r, g, x), sec_route_param(g, x, p), sec_key(p, k).
// The functions holding this rule's sinks: a validator-named helper that itself filters or orders is no check.
sec_sink_fn(gq) :- olk_name_arg(c, _, q), sec_bres(q), nearest(c, g, fdef), pt_def(g, gq).
sec_sink_fn(gq) :- olk_splat(c, _, q), sec_bres(q), nearest(c, g, fdef), pt_def(g, gq).
// Across files: what a call passes unchecked, what a function returns unchecked; a check call of the run passes it
// through a gate (sec_egate of lib/security's "sec" checks).
sec_froute("olks", "seg"). sec_froute("olks", "free").
sec_fpass("olks", c, a, o) :- call_arg(c, _, _, a), olk_str(a, o), !sec_checked_expr(a), !sec_echk_any("sec", a).
sec_fpass("olks", c, a, g) :- call_arg(c, _, _, a), olk_str(a, _), !sec_checked_expr(a), sec_egate("sec", "olks", a, g).
sec_gin(g, o) :- call_arg(_, _, _, a), olk_str(a, o), !sec_checked_expr(a), sec_egate("sec", "olks", a, g).
sec_fctx("olks", c, o) :- call_arg(c, _, _, a), olk_str(a, o).
sec_fret("olks", g, o) :- olk_ret(g, v), olk_str(v, o), !sec_echk_any("sec", v).
sec_fret("olks", g, eg) :- olk_ret(g, v), olk_str(v, _), sec_egate("sec", "olks", v, eg).
sec_gin(eg, o) :- olk_ret(g, v), olk_str(v, o), sec_egate("sec", "olks", v, eg).
.decl olk_ret(g: node, v: node)
olk_ret(g, v) :- kind(r, "return_statement"), child(r, v, 0), nearest(r, g, fdef), !sec_checked_expr(v).

// olk_keys(e, o): e is a mapping whose keys the client chose, from origin o: the request's own mappings and what is
// read off them, a dict or comprehension with a request-derived key, a name filled with such keys, a parameter given
// one (`P|olkk|…`), a call of a function of the run that returns one (`R|olkk|…`). Not `self.kwargs`: its keys are
// the URLconf's capture names (its values are text, olk_str).
.decl olk_keys(e: node, o: symbol)
olk_keys(e, k) :- sec_source(e, _), sec_key(e, k).
olk_keys(e, o) :- sec_stepg(e, a), olk_key_step(e), olk_keys(a, o).
olk_keys(e, g) :- sec_stepq("olkk", e, a, g), olk_key_step(e), olk_keys(a, _).
sec_gin(g, o) :- sec_stepq("olkk", e, a, g), olk_key_step(e), olk_keys(a, o).
olk_keys(t, o) :- kind(t, "dictionary"), child(t, p, _), kind(p, "pair"), field(p, "key", k), olk_str(k, o).
olk_keys(t, o) :- kind(t, "dictionary"), child(t, sp, _), kind(sp, "dictionary_splat"), child(sp, a, 0),
    olk_keys(a, o).
olk_keys(t, o) :- kind(t, "dictionary_comprehension"), field(t, "body", p), field(p, "key", k), olk_str(k, o).
olk_keys(r, o) :- olk_kin(r, o), olk_ref(r, h, x), !sec_nchk_any("olk", h, x).
olk_keys(r, g) :- olk_kin(r, _), olk_ref(r, h, x), sec_ngate("olk", "olkk", h, x, g).
sec_gin(g, o) :- olk_kin(r, o), olk_ref(r, h, x), sec_ngate("olk", "olkk", h, x, g).
olk_keys(c, o) :- sec_rorig(c, "olkk", o).
// olk_kin(r, o): name r reads keys o before its checks: a value bound to it, keys stored into it, a parameter's, a
// FastAPI route's dict parameter.
.decl olk_kin(r: node, o: symbol)
olk_kin(r, o) :- kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, x), look(r, x, h), sec_bind(h, x, v), r != v, olk_keys(v, o).
olk_kin(r, o) :- kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, x), look(r, x, h), olk_key_store(h, x, o).
olk_kin(r, o) :- sec_porig(r, "olkk", _, _, o).
olk_kin(r, k) :- sec_param_ref(r, g, x), sec_route_param(g, x, p), olk_dict_param(g, p), sec_key(p, k).
// olk_dict_param(g, p): parameter p of g is annotated as a mapping (`dict`, `Dict`, `Any`, Optional of one).
.decl olk_dict_param(g: node, p: node)
olk_dict_param(g, p) :- sig_param(g, p, _, _, _, an, _), text(an, t), match("(typing\\.)?(Optional\\[)?\\s*(dict|Dict|Any)\\b.*", t).
// A Django view's capture holds keys when its parameter is so annotated (olk_dict_q, in the view's file).
.decl olk_dict_q(g: symbol, x: symbol)
olk_dict_q(gq, x) :- olk_dict_param(g, p), sig_param(g, p, nm, _, _, _, _), text(nm, x), pt_def(g, gq).
sec_xparam("olkk", gq, x, k) :- sec_xdj_param(gq, x, k, _), olk_dict_q(gq, x).
sec_fpass("olkk", c, a, o) :- call_arg(c, _, _, a), olk_keys(a, o), !sec_checked_expr(a), !sec_echk_any("sec", a).
sec_fpass("olkk", c, a, g) :- call_arg(c, _, _, a), olk_keys(a, _), !sec_checked_expr(a), sec_egate("sec", "olkk", a, g).
sec_gin(g, o) :- call_arg(_, _, _, a), olk_keys(a, o), !sec_checked_expr(a), sec_egate("sec", "olkk", a, g).
sec_fctx("olkk", c, o) :- call_arg(c, _, _, a), (olk_keys(a, o) ; olk_str(a, o)).
sec_fret("olkk", g, o) :- kind(r, "return_statement"), child(r, v, 0), nearest(r, g, fdef), olk_keys(v, o).
// olk_key_step(e): the steps that keep a mapping's keys: reading off it (`.dict()`, `.copy()`, `["filters"]`,
// `.get("filters")`), awaiting it, parentheses, a conditional or `or`; not a validated form's or serializer's data.
.decl olk_key_step(e: node)
olk_key_step(e) :- kind(e, "subscript"). olk_key_step(e) :- kind(e, "call"). olk_key_step(e) :- kind(e, "await").
olk_key_step(e) :- kind(e, "parenthesized_expression"). olk_key_step(e) :- kind(e, "conditional_expression").
olk_key_step(e) :- kind(e, "boolean_operator").
olk_key_step(e) :- attr_of(e, _, m), !sec_validated_attr(m).
// olk_key_store(h, x, o): scope h stores a client-chosen key into name x: `x[key] = …`, `x.update(<request
// mapping>)`, `x.update(**<request mapping>)`.
.decl olk_key_store(h: node, x: symbol, o: symbol)
olk_key_store(h, x, o) :- kind(a, "assignment"), field(a, "left", l), kind(l, "subscript"), field(l, "value", b),
    kind(b, "identifier"), text(b, x), field(l, "subscript", k), olk_str(k, o), nearest(a, h, scope).
olk_key_store(h, x, o) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, b, "update"), kind(b, "identifier"),
    text(b, x), sec_arg(c, 0, "", a), olk_keys(a, o), nearest(c, h, scope).
olk_key_store(h, x, o) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, b, "update"), kind(b, "identifier"),
    text(b, x), olk_kwsplat(c, a), olk_keys(a, o), nearest(c, h, scope).

// The cases, `cases/python-security-orm-lookup-injection/`, read as one repository: each line ending in `# caught`
// is reported, and no other line.
.test cases exactly
    .fixture "catalog/__init__.py" from "../cases/python-security-orm-lookup-injection/catalog/__init__.py"
    .fixture "catalog/admin_views.py" from "../cases/python-security-orm-lookup-injection/catalog/admin_views.py"
    .fixture "catalog/api.py" from "../cases/python-security-orm-lookup-injection/catalog/api.py"
    .fixture "catalog/browse.py" from "../cases/python-security-orm-lookup-injection/catalog/browse.py"
    .fixture "catalog/helpers.py" from "../cases/python-security-orm-lookup-injection/catalog/helpers.py"
    .fixture "catalog/keys.py" from "../cases/python-security-orm-lookup-injection/catalog/keys.py"
    .fixture "catalog/models.py" from "../cases/python-security-orm-lookup-injection/catalog/models.py"
    .fixture "catalog/queries.py" from "../cases/python-security-orm-lookup-injection/catalog/queries.py"
    .fixture "catalog/routed.py" from "../cases/python-security-orm-lookup-injection/catalog/routed.py"
    .fixture "catalog/tests/__init__.py" from "../cases/python-security-orm-lookup-injection/catalog/tests/__init__.py"
    .fixture "catalog/tests/test_views.py" from "../cases/python-security-orm-lookup-injection/catalog/tests/test_views.py"
    .fixture "catalog/urls.py" from "../cases/python-security-orm-lookup-injection/catalog/urls.py"
    .fixture "catalog/validated.py" from "../cases/python-security-orm-lookup-injection/catalog/validated.py"
    .fixture "catalog/views.py" from "../cases/python-security-orm-lookup-injection/catalog/views.py"
